 =20
  <p style=3D"margin: 16px 0;"><strong>The major agents already speak OpenR=
outer.</strong></p>
 =20

   =20
 =20
  <p style=3D"margin: 16px 0;"><strong>Cursor.</strong> Drop your OpenRoute=
r key into Settings and pick any model from the dropdown. Switch between Cl=
aude, GPT, Gemini, and DeepSeek per task without leaving the editor.<br/><s=
trong>Cline.</strong> Autonomous coding with auto-routing. The agent picks =
the right model per step, so planning runs on a thinking model and executio=
n runs on something faster and cheaper.<br/><strong>Continue.</strong> Open=
-source, configurable. Point the base URL at OpenRouter and every model is =
available from the model picker.<br/><strong>Claude Code.</strong> Use Open=
Router as the backend to track team usage, set per-key rate limits, and con=
trol spend across models without touching Anthropic billing directly.</p>
 =20

   =20
 =20
  <p style=3D"margin: 16px 0;"><strong>Why the multi-model swap matters for=
 agents.</strong> Most coding agents are cheaper and faster when you route =
structured steps like file reads and diff writes to a small model, and rese=
rve a frontier model for the part that actually writes code. The cost gap b=
etween a $0.15/M token small model and a $15/M token frontier model stacks =
up fast when the agent makes 50 calls per task.</p>
 =20

   =20
 =20
  <p style=3D"margin: 16px 0;"><strong>Usage visibility.</strong> The activ=
ity dashboard shows every request with its model, cost, latency, and token =
counts. If an agent runs away, you see it inside minutes, not at the end of=
 a billing cycle. Per-key rate limits stop the bleeding without disabling t=
he whole integration.</p>
 =20

